(DeepResidualAttention: Enhanced Multi-Scale Representations in Deep Vision Models) Tj
0 -18 Td (Authors: Dr. Elena Vance and Prof. Marcus Chen) Tj
0 -18 Td (Abstract: Recent convolutional and vision transformer architectures demonstrate notable achievements) Tj
0 -18 Td (in visual recognition. However, multi-scale feature degradation remains a critical challenge.) Tj
0 -18 Td (We propose DeepResidualAttention [DRA], a novel hierarchical attention mechanism that dynamically) Tj
0 -18 Td (balances spatial and channel-wise feature dependencies across distinct resolution scales.) Tj
0 -18 Td (Our empirical evaluations on ImageNet-1K demonstrate that DRA achieves a top-1 accuracy improvement) Tj
0 -18 Td (of 2.4 percent over ResNet-50 and 1.8 percent over Swin-T while reducing parameter count by 14.3 percent.) Tj
0 -18 Td (1. Introduction and Research Problem:) Tj
0 -18 Td (Deep residual networks rely on identity shortcut connections to alleviate gradient vanishing.) Tj
0 -18 Td (Despite their success, deep features suffer from semantic attenuation as network depth scales.) Tj
0 -18 Td (Existing spatial attention mechanisms often fail to capture long-range contextual relationships) Tj
0 -18 Td (without introducing quadratic computational overhead. The primary research challenge is formulating) Tj
0 -18 Td (a multi-scale attention weighting function that balances efficiency with representation power.) Tj
ET
endstream
