(3. Experimental Setup and Quantitative Results:) Tj
0 -18 Td (We evaluate DRA on ImageNet-1K [1.28 million training images, 50,000 validation images] and MS-COCO.) Tj
0 -18 Td (Models are trained using AdamW optimizer with initial learning rate of 1e-4, cosine annealing) Tj
0 -18 Td (over 300 epochs, batch size 256, and weight decay 0.05 on 8 NVIDIA A100 GPUs.) Tj
0 -18 Td (Benchmark Comparison on ImageNet-1K:) Tj
0 -18 Td (- ResNet-50 Baseline: 76.1 percent Top-1 Accuracy, 25.6M Parameters, 4.1 GFLOPs.) Tj
0 -18 Td (- Swin-T Baseline: 81.3 percent Top-1 Accuracy, 28.3M Parameters, 4.5 GFLOPs.) Tj
0 -18 Td (- DRA [Proposed]: 83.1 percent Top-1 Accuracy, 24.2M Parameters, 3.9 GFLOPs.) Tj
0 -18 Td (Ablation Studies:) Tj
0 -18 Td (Removing cross-scale residual highway causes an immediate 1.7 percent drop in Top-1 accuracy,) Tj
0 -18 Td (proving that inter-stage gradient communication is pivotal.) Tj
0 -18 Td (4. Limitations and Threats to Validity:) Tj
0 -18 Td (Although DRA reduces parameter count and FLOPs, memory footprint during training is approximately) Tj
0 -18 Td (11 percent higher due to caching intermediate activation maps for cross-scale gating.) Tj
0 -18 Td (5. Conclusion:) Tj
0 -18 Td (DeepResidualAttention establishes that decoupled cross-scale attention gating achieves state-of-the-art) Tj
0 -18 Td (accuracy with improved parameter efficiency. Future work will investigate edge deployment quantization.) Tj
ET
